1
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:52,111
Hey!

2
00:01:57,651 --> 00:02:00,451
Straw Hat Luffy, you're out!

3
00:02:00,531 --> 00:02:01,531
What?

4
00:02:02,291 --> 00:02:03,751
It's over!

5
00:02:03,831 --> 00:02:06,551
Straw Hat Luffy has eeped his way to defeat

6
00:02:06,631 --> 00:02:10,091
as Team Foxy claims victory in the first round!

7
00:02:12,471 --> 00:02:15,431
Showdown on the cliff, red light, green light.

8
00:02:15,431 --> 00:02:20,431
The Foxy Pirates have claimed the victory for round one

9
00:02:20,511 --> 00:02:22,731
in the rematch of the Davy Mac fight.

10
00:02:22,811 --> 00:02:25,071
It's time for the boss to claim his prize.

11
00:02:25,151 --> 00:02:28,571
Which member of the Straw Hat crew will he choose?

12
00:02:28,651 --> 00:02:30,071
The one I want is.

13
00:02:30,151 --> 00:02:33,411
Oh, it's so obvious, isn't it, boss?

14
00:02:33,491 --> 00:02:38,451
You! The archaeologist Nicarabind!

15
00:02:38,531 --> 00:02:40,131
You want me?

16
00:02:40,191 --> 00:02:41,391
Oh!

17
00:02:41,391 --> 00:02:43,051
Oh, the boss has decided that his pick

18
00:02:43,131 --> 00:02:44,691
for this round is Nico Robin!

19
00:02:44,771 --> 00:02:47,031
Oh, Captain, you're such a naughty boy.

20
00:02:47,131 --> 00:02:48,231
Why, boss?

21
00:02:48,331 --> 00:02:50,871
Why didn't you get my adorable little choppy back?

22
00:02:50,971 --> 00:02:53,311
We can't afford to leave that woman on the Straw Hat's team.

23
00:02:53,411 --> 00:02:54,831
She's far too dangerous.

24
00:02:54,931 --> 00:02:56,871
Bringing her to our side will give us the advantage

25
00:02:56,971 --> 00:02:58,071
from here on out.

26
00:02:58,171 --> 00:02:58,911
But...

27
00:02:59,011 --> 00:03:01,071
This way, taking Dr. Chopper back in the next round

28
00:03:01,171 --> 00:03:02,811
will be a piece of cake.

29
00:03:02,911 --> 00:03:04,251
Now I get it.

30
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:05,611
You're so smart, boss.

31
00:03:05,711 --> 00:03:07,091
Faith, it's the best.

32
00:03:07,191 --> 00:03:08,451
You're so smart, boss.

33
00:03:08,451 --> 00:03:09,251
Oh, I get it.

34
00:03:09,351 --> 00:03:10,391
You're so smart, boss.

35
00:03:10,491 --> 00:03:12,291
Faith, it's the best.

36
00:03:12,391 --> 00:03:13,451
Robin!

37
00:03:13,551 --> 00:03:15,191
Robin, my love!

38
00:03:15,291 --> 00:03:16,391
See you later.

39
00:03:18,491 --> 00:03:20,291
I feel her pain.

40
00:03:20,391 --> 00:03:21,691
She's trying to hide her sorrow

41
00:03:21,791 --> 00:03:23,591
behind that beautiful smile.

42
00:03:23,691 --> 00:03:25,671
She hates being apart from me.

43
00:03:25,771 --> 00:03:27,771
How dare they take my sweet ramen away?

44
00:03:27,871 --> 00:03:30,331
Even if it's the rules, do they know nothing of love?

45
00:03:30,431 --> 00:03:31,671
Robin!

46
00:03:31,771 --> 00:03:32,771
Robin!

47
00:03:35,471 --> 00:03:36,671
So, how does it look?

48
00:03:36,771 --> 00:03:37,511
Splendid.

49
00:03:37,511 --> 00:03:39,711
Perfect, it complements that beautiful hair.

50
00:03:39,811 --> 00:03:41,851
You were the one we wanted from the beginning.

51
00:03:41,951 --> 00:03:43,511
Aw, she's so popular.

52
00:03:45,351 --> 00:03:46,751
She, uh...

53
00:03:46,851 --> 00:03:49,451
She seems to be getting along with them pretty well.

54
00:03:49,551 --> 00:03:50,251
It figures.

55
00:03:50,351 --> 00:03:52,451
I never trusted that woman to begin with.

56
00:03:52,551 --> 00:03:53,731
What are you talking about?

57
00:03:53,831 --> 00:03:55,291
Robin trusts us to get her back.

58
00:03:55,391 --> 00:03:57,371
That's all, I think.

59
00:03:57,471 --> 00:03:59,531
As always, Nami's right on the money.

60
00:03:59,631 --> 00:04:01,731
I'm gonna give it everything I've got in the next round

61
00:04:01,831 --> 00:04:03,631
and help win Robin back for us.

62
00:04:03,731 --> 00:04:05,471
Let's get this next round going!

63
00:04:05,571 --> 00:04:06,511
Let me at him!

64
00:04:06,511 --> 00:04:08,611
Luffy, you can't compete in the next round.

65
00:04:08,711 --> 00:04:10,451
You're in the third round, remember?

66
00:04:10,551 --> 00:04:12,651
Geez, just remember the rules already.

67
00:04:12,751 --> 00:04:15,011
All right, guess I'm on cheering duty then.

68
00:04:15,111 --> 00:04:17,351
With Robin gone, that means there are only five of us

69
00:04:17,451 --> 00:04:18,451
in the next event.

70
00:04:18,551 --> 00:04:21,651
Stupid straw hats.

71
00:04:21,751 --> 00:04:23,631
You've lost more than a member of your crew.

72
00:04:23,731 --> 00:04:25,571
You've lost a major part of your offense.

73
00:04:25,671 --> 00:04:26,971
How do you like them grapes?

74
00:04:27,071 --> 00:04:28,971
Or apples, whatever.

75
00:04:29,071 --> 00:04:30,371
On to the next event.

76
00:04:30,371 --> 00:04:37,351
Fell, fell, fell, fell, fell, fell, fell, fell, fell.

77
00:04:37,451 --> 00:04:39,411
Round two will be held on the long reef.

78
00:04:39,511 --> 00:04:44,311
The game will be Dash Touch Domination or DTD for short.

79
00:04:44,411 --> 00:04:46,591
Although this is a six on six group competition,

80
00:04:46,691 --> 00:04:48,991
the absence of Nico Robin forces the Straw Hats

81
00:04:48,991 --> 00:04:51,931
the Straw Hats to compete with only five players.

82
00:04:51,931 --> 00:04:54,871
The rules are simple, basically it's played the same way

83
00:04:54,871 --> 00:04:56,531
as the game Red Light, Green Light.

84
00:04:56,531 --> 00:04:58,591
Whoever moves even just the tiniest little bit

85
00:04:58,591 --> 00:05:00,851
after the light stops calling is out.

86
00:05:00,851 --> 00:05:03,211
Whichever team touches the stoplight at the top

87
00:05:03,211 --> 00:05:05,431
of the reef first will be declared the winner.

88
00:05:05,431 --> 00:05:07,051
But this is no kid's game.

89
00:05:07,051 --> 00:05:09,531
Remember, when pirates play Red Light, Green Light,

90
00:05:09,531 --> 00:05:11,511
they play hard and they play to win.

91
00:05:11,511 --> 00:05:13,931
The use of weapons is approved and encouraged.

92
00:05:13,931 --> 00:05:18,091
This is what makes DTT a truly perilous game.

93
00:05:18,091 --> 00:05:20,191
Playing for the Straw Hat team is,

94
00:05:20,191 --> 00:05:21,871
the same boring lineup as always.

95
00:05:21,871 --> 00:05:23,211
Shut it, jerk!

96
00:05:23,211 --> 00:05:25,911
Leading off for Team Foxy is our beloved idol,

97
00:05:25,911 --> 00:05:28,451
Parcha, and the beastly oddity, Hamburr.

98
00:05:28,451 --> 00:05:30,871
Soon I will have Little Choppy right back in my hand.

99
00:05:30,871 --> 00:05:32,331
Boop, boop, boop, boop, boop, boop, boop.

100
00:05:32,331 --> 00:05:34,091
The rest of the team consists of the

101
00:05:34,091 --> 00:05:36,951
Everswift Chicky Cheetah, the Fishman Capote,

102
00:05:36,951 --> 00:05:39,651
and back for some vengeance for their loss in the groggy ring,

103
00:05:39,651 --> 00:05:43,511
we have Tackle Machine Pickles and Big Panda Wotan.

104
00:05:43,511 --> 00:05:45,711
We're gonna make those Straw Hat losers pay

105
00:05:45,711 --> 00:05:47,151
for humiliating us.

106
00:05:47,151 --> 00:05:51,551
These six competitors will make Team Foxy

107
00:05:51,551 --> 00:05:54,191
a force to be reckoned with.

108
00:05:54,191 --> 00:05:56,291
Hey, why's the old Stiltzke

109
00:05:56,291 --> 00:05:57,911
up there, riding around with him?

110
00:05:57,911 --> 00:06:00,111
And last but not least, the role of our stoplight

111
00:06:00,111 --> 00:06:03,551
will be played by none other than the nomad himself Kamsiek.

112
00:06:03,551 --> 00:06:05,231
This great fool, I mean man of bravery,

113
00:06:05,231 --> 00:06:07,891
stood atop Stiltz for ten years to touch the heavens.

114
00:06:07,891 --> 00:06:09,871
This makes him the logical choice to stand

115
00:06:09,871 --> 00:06:11,551
at the top of the reef and be it!

116
00:06:11,551 --> 00:06:14,631
I'm seriously sick and tired of high places, though.

117
00:06:14,631 --> 00:06:19,731
Hey, wait a minute. If the old man is the stoplight, that gives us a big advantage in the DTD.

118
00:06:19,731 --> 00:06:22,131
Uh, let's not get ahead of ourselves here.

119
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:25,631
But who stops right, you guys? This could be just the lucky break that we meet.

120
00:06:27,631 --> 00:06:29,631
You sure about all this, Captain?

121
00:06:29,631 --> 00:06:36,631
Come on, this is nothing! If our crew is strong enough to battle the treacherous wide open sea, then this is child's play! Don't sweat this small stuff!

122
00:06:37,631 --> 00:06:38,631
You said it, boss!

123
00:06:38,631 --> 00:06:40,631
Yeah, our captain's the greatest!

124
00:06:40,631 --> 00:06:47,631
Child's play, huh? Then why did you give us this unfair, docked-up course giving you the advantage from the start?

125
00:06:51,631 --> 00:06:54,631
I guess using that dodo beam really is his only talent.

126
00:06:54,631 --> 00:06:55,631
Stupid fox!

127
00:06:55,631 --> 00:06:56,631
Split head!

128
00:06:57,631 --> 00:07:01,631
Hey, dodo beam! I'm the stupid fox! Split head!

129
00:07:01,631 --> 00:07:02,631
Boss, no!

130
00:07:02,631 --> 00:07:03,631
Listen to them!

131
00:07:03,631 --> 00:07:06,631
You certainly wear your heart on your sleeve, Captain Foxy.

132
00:07:06,631 --> 00:07:12,631
To kick off this event as the DTD rules state, both teams must start by calling out the first step!

133
00:07:12,631 --> 00:07:14,631
Taking the first step, now!

134
00:07:15,631 --> 00:07:19,631
So it begins! And Captain Foxy is already off to an early lead!

135
00:07:19,631 --> 00:07:21,631
It's because of those huge freaks.

136
00:07:21,631 --> 00:07:25,631
If we follow the boss's plan, this'll be easy! Let's do it!

137
00:07:25,631 --> 00:07:26,631
Yeah!

138
00:07:26,631 --> 00:07:31,631
I'm sure this goes without saying, but there's more to winning this thing than just being the first one to touch the stoplight.

139
00:07:31,631 --> 00:07:38,631
This twisted terrain makes it easy to lose your balance when coming to a sudden stop, so that'll be the most likely time for the enemy to attack.

140
00:07:38,631 --> 00:07:43,631
Hey, split head! If you screw around with this race, I'm gonna have something to say about it!

141
00:07:43,631 --> 00:07:44,631
Split head?

142
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:49,631
Like I'd even need to interfere! We could win this race in our sleeves, straw hat!

143
00:07:49,631 --> 00:07:51,631
Stoplight! Are you ready to begin?

144
00:07:51,631 --> 00:07:52,631
Uh-huh!

145
00:07:52,631 --> 00:07:54,631
Then take your position!

146
00:07:55,631 --> 00:07:56,631
Yeah!

147
00:07:56,631 --> 00:07:57,631
Yeah!

148
00:07:59,631 --> 00:08:02,631
To recap, Team Foxy claimed the victory in the last round!

149
00:08:02,631 --> 00:08:05,631
Let's see what happens in round two, DTD!

150
00:08:05,631 --> 00:08:07,631
Ready, go!

151
00:08:08,631 --> 00:08:10,631
Green!

152
00:08:10,631 --> 00:08:16,631
Run! Quick, Hamburg!

153
00:08:17,631 --> 00:08:22,631
Cheeky Cheetah sprints ahead to take an early lead with Full Dash Hamburg following behind in second place!

154
00:08:22,631 --> 00:08:27,631
Meanwhile, on the straw hat side, Zoro and Zanji are out in front running neck and neck!

155
00:08:27,631 --> 00:08:28,631
Move! You're in the way!

156
00:08:28,631 --> 00:08:30,631
No, you move! You're in my way!

157
00:08:30,631 --> 00:08:32,631
How can those two idiots run and argue at the same time?

158
00:08:32,631 --> 00:08:34,631
Hey! Knock it off, you two!

159
00:08:34,631 --> 00:08:36,631
Yeah! Concentrate on the game!

160
00:08:36,631 --> 00:08:38,631
They're amazing!

161
00:08:39,631 --> 00:08:40,631
Night!

162
00:08:43,631 --> 00:08:44,631
What the heck?!

163
00:08:44,631 --> 00:08:48,631
How could you hold that word out for so long, freaky old stilts guy?!

164
00:08:48,631 --> 00:08:50,631
He makes an ideal stoplight!

165
00:08:50,631 --> 00:08:53,631
Red!

166
00:08:54,631 --> 00:08:55,631
Let me die, loser!

167
00:08:55,631 --> 00:08:56,631
What was that, fist-flake head?!

168
00:08:56,631 --> 00:08:58,631
You hurt me!

169
00:08:59,631 --> 00:09:02,631
The only ones to worry about from the straw hat team are those two!

170
00:09:02,631 --> 00:09:05,631
Let's knock them out of the game quick, just like we planned!

171
00:09:06,631 --> 00:09:07,851
This is it.

172
00:09:07,931 --> 00:09:09,351
It can!

173
00:09:13,351 --> 00:09:15,351
Spunk attack!

174
00:09:17,351 --> 00:09:19,111
Oh, crap, it's headed right for him!

175
00:09:19,191 --> 00:09:21,191
And the old man's about to finish his red light!

176
00:09:21,271 --> 00:09:23,031
We don't have time to worry about that!

177
00:09:23,111 --> 00:09:25,691
I...

178
00:09:29,731 --> 00:09:30,691
This is it.

179
00:09:31,911 --> 00:09:34,111
I...

180
00:09:34,111 --> 00:09:36,831
Quick, stop me!

181
00:09:50,831 --> 00:09:53,471
If we move, we'll be out!

182
00:10:00,511 --> 00:10:01,631
You're out.

183
00:10:01,631 --> 00:10:05,151
An early upset on Team Foxy for Pickles and Big Fan!

184
00:10:05,231 --> 00:10:07,391
They've been knocked off the course and out of the game!

185
00:10:07,471 --> 00:10:10,191
All right, Zoro and Soji! Way to go! Nice one!

186
00:10:10,271 --> 00:10:11,871
Whatever! It's no big deal!

187
00:10:11,951 --> 00:10:15,071
We only need one person on Team Foxy to touch him for the win,

188
00:10:15,151 --> 00:10:17,151
and it doesn't matter which one of them does it!

189
00:10:17,231 --> 00:10:18,351
Perfect!

190
00:10:19,311 --> 00:10:22,111
Chicky Cheetah, Port Cha, and Hamburg are out in front

191
00:10:22,191 --> 00:10:24,911
and have quite a significant lead over the straw hats!

192
00:10:24,911 --> 00:10:28,031
Oh, my! That put me in a weird totally-gonna-win mood!

193
00:10:30,351 --> 00:10:31,791
Damn, they're way too fast!

194
00:10:31,871 --> 00:10:34,591
It looks like Zoro and Sanji are our only hope!

195
00:10:34,671 --> 00:10:36,591
Stupid moss head, sword swinger!

196
00:10:36,671 --> 00:10:38,271
Delusional love cook!

197
00:10:38,351 --> 00:10:40,511
I'm warning you, I'm on a very important mission

198
00:10:40,591 --> 00:10:41,951
to rescue my sweet Robin.

199
00:10:42,031 --> 00:10:44,031
If you do anything to get in the way,

200
00:10:44,111 --> 00:10:46,191
I don't have time to listen to this crap!

201
00:10:46,191 --> 00:10:49,471
Hey! Hold on! I wasn't finished, you jerk!

202
00:10:52,111 --> 00:10:53,791
Despite losing two players,

203
00:10:53,871 --> 00:10:55,471
Team Foxy has a huge lead

204
00:10:55,551 --> 00:10:57,711
and is the closest to reaching the stoplight!

205
00:10:57,791 --> 00:11:00,031
At this rate, the straw hats don't stand a chance

206
00:11:00,111 --> 00:11:01,151
of winning this round!

207
00:11:04,591 --> 00:11:06,031
Go! Go!

208
00:11:06,111 --> 00:11:07,791
That's it, yes, just like that!

209
00:11:07,871 --> 00:11:09,071
Keep it up and we'll win!

210
00:11:16,191 --> 00:11:18,351
Team Foxy has a huge lead

211
00:11:28,991 --> 00:11:31,151
Dammit, it's your fault we've fallen so far behind,

212
00:11:31,151 --> 00:11:32,271
you stupid moss head!

213
00:11:32,271 --> 00:11:33,631
If we lose this round, I'm...

214
00:11:36,191 --> 00:11:37,151
How'd this happen?

215
00:11:37,791 --> 00:11:38,911
The path is gone!

216
00:11:39,551 --> 00:11:42,191
How in the hell can anyone get lost on a path like this one?

217
00:11:42,191 --> 00:11:44,111
You can see the old man at the end of it!

218
00:11:44,111 --> 00:11:46,431
Even your sense of direction can't be that bad!

219
00:11:50,111 --> 00:11:52,671
I can make up some time if I use this as a shortcut.

220
00:11:53,311 --> 00:11:54,911
It's risky, but it's do or die.

221
00:11:58,511 --> 00:12:00,911
Looks like Sanji is taking a huge gamble!

222
00:12:03,871 --> 00:12:04,511
Close one.

223
00:12:08,591 --> 00:12:11,151
It seems that Sanji's big gamble has paid off!

224
00:12:11,151 --> 00:12:13,711
Now he's right behind the lead group and closing in fast!

225
00:12:13,711 --> 00:12:14,591
Not fair!

226
00:12:14,591 --> 00:12:15,711
Hey, Berg, hurry!

227
00:12:15,711 --> 00:12:16,831
He's gaining on us!

228
00:12:18,831 --> 00:12:19,391
What?

229
00:12:19,391 --> 00:12:20,031
What do you want?

230
00:12:21,631 --> 00:12:25,151
In my opinion, it never hurts to reduce the number of opponents you have.

231
00:12:25,151 --> 00:12:27,151
Time for the three of you to kick the button.

232
00:12:28,111 --> 00:12:29,071
Oh, crap!

233
00:12:29,071 --> 00:12:30,191
Nami, you stop!

234
00:12:30,191 --> 00:12:31,391
What do we do?

235
00:12:31,391 --> 00:12:32,511
We have no choice.

236
00:12:33,871 --> 00:12:35,231
Everybody run for it!

237
00:12:35,231 --> 00:12:36,191
Butcher!

238
00:12:36,191 --> 00:12:37,311
Hey, get back here!

239
00:12:37,311 --> 00:12:38,431
You can't escape from me!

240
00:12:38,431 --> 00:12:39,391
Yeah!

241
00:12:39,391 --> 00:12:40,831
Yee-yah!

242
00:12:40,831 --> 00:12:41,631
Come here!

243
00:12:41,631 --> 00:12:42,511
Now!

244
00:12:42,511 --> 00:12:48,031
Man, the old stilts guy's green is even longer than it was last time.

245
00:12:48,031 --> 00:12:52,911
He's sleeping?

246
00:12:52,911 --> 00:12:53,631
Hey!

247
00:12:53,631 --> 00:12:54,911
Wake up!

248
00:12:54,911 --> 00:12:55,951
Wake up!

249
00:12:55,951 --> 00:12:56,911
Don't be sleeping!

250
00:12:56,911 --> 00:12:58,911
Green light, red light, stop!

251
00:12:58,911 --> 00:12:59,791
Let's do it!

252
00:12:59,791 --> 00:13:00,991
Let's do it!

253
00:13:00,991 --> 00:13:01,791
Ah!

254
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:02,511
Ah!

255
00:13:02,511 --> 00:13:03,311
Ah!

256
00:13:03,311 --> 00:13:04,111
Ah!

257
00:13:04,111 --> 00:13:04,591
Ah!

258
00:13:04,591 --> 00:13:05,391
Ah!

259
00:13:05,391 --> 00:13:06,351
Ah!

